# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

Fill Classic+'s card animation table so that 73 of its 78 cards and 19 of its tokens have an entry other than `none`. Every Spell, Field Spell, Trap and Field Trap gets its `cast` (or keeps its set piece or bespoke key), and every Field Spell gets an `aura`. Add one new motif, `deal`, under the three-card rule, and three new bespoke Flourishes alongside Crushing Walls; each Flourish gets a vitest and an R200 check. Make `/dev/fx` play every Classic+ entry. A per-set test enforces the measure and R202. The deliverable is the per-card PR table.

## Files to touch

| Path | | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/fx/cards/classicplus.json5` | change | every entry (Step 8) |
| `apps/web/src/fx/cards/classicplus/rollback.ts` | new | `rollbackSweep` |
| `apps/web/src/fx/cards/classicplus/kysConstant.ts` | new | `constantStamp` |
| `apps/web/src/fx/cards/classicplus/bookOfPain.ts` | new | `inkTear` |
| `apps/web/src/fx/cards/classicplus/flourishes.test.ts` | new | Flourish tests |
| `apps/web/src/fx/cards/classicplus.test.ts` | new | per-set test |
| `apps/web/src/fx/cards/bespoke.ts` | change | register 3 recipes in `CARD_RECIPES` |
| `apps/web/src/fx/cards/tables.test.ts` | change | R2787000 ten-Field-Spell assertion |
| `apps/web/src/fx/motifs/names.ts` | change | `deal` |
| `apps/web/src/fx/motifs/hand.ts` | change | `deal` planner |
| `apps/web/src/fx/motifs/index.ts` | change | `MOTIF_PLANNERS.deal` |
| `apps/web/src/fx/motifs/gallery.ts` | change | `deal` fixture, `GalleryCard` helpers |
| `apps/web/src/fx/motifs/motifs.test.ts` | change | `PINNED.deal`, deal test |
| `apps/web/src/fx/constants.ts`, `constants.test.ts` | change | 3 constants, `FX_MOTIF_TRAUMA.deal` |
| `apps/web/src/routes/dev/fx.tsx`, `fx.test.tsx` | change | gallery plays every entry |
| `docs/polish/9-card-animations.md` | change | deal row, Flourishes, gallery, census note |
| `spec/rulings/R2795000.md`, `spec/pending/2795.md` | new | ruling and its §11 paragraph |

Do not touch: `crates/`, other sets' `.json5`, `fx/takeover.ts`, `entrances.ts`, `cardFx.ts`, `spec/11-rulings.md`, `spec/INDEX.md`, `.github/`, `.harness/`, `bot/`. Governing rules: §10.10, R200, R201, R202, R2784000, R2787000, R2800000, R2785000; R2722000–R2722002 stay unchanged.

## Steps

1. **`fx/constants.ts`**:
   - Next to `FX_MOTIF_TITHE_MAX`, add `export const FX_MOTIF_DEAL_MAX = 5; // deal: the cards one entry deals`.
   - Add `deal: 0` after `snap` in `FX_MOTIF_TRAUMA`.
   - After the `FX_WALLS_*` lines, add `export const FX_ROLLBACK_STEP = 0.08;` (Rollback: the fraction of D between lane rings) and `export const FX_INK_TEAR_TRAUMA = 0.2;`.
   - Pin all four in `constants.test.ts`'s `S2` object, at the same positions.

2. **`motifs/names.ts`**: insert `"deal"` after `"snap"` in `FX_MOTIF_NAMES` (before `"aura"`) and append it after `"snap"` in `FX_DRAWN_MOTIFS`.

3. **`motifs/hand.ts`**: add the planner. Import `sourceOf` and `flies` from `./build.ts`, `testid` from `../../game/contract.ts`, and `FX_MOTIF_DEAL_MAX`.
   ```ts
   const DEAL_READS = ["addedToHand", "shuffledIn", "fused"] as const;
   /** Where a dealt card comes from: the resolving play's hero, else the hero it goes to; none for a fuse. */
   function dealtFrom(event: GameEvent, view: PlayerView, env: FxPlanEnv): FxAnchor | null {
     const from = sourceOf(event, view, env);
     if (from !== null) return from;
     return event.type === "addedToHand" || event.type === "shuffledIn" ? tid(testid.hero(sideOf(view, event.player))) : null;
   }
   /** deal (R2795000): a card back from the source to the hand, the library or the card it fuses into, landing with a sparkle; its rows still play. */
   export const deal: MotifPlanner = {
     reads: DEAL_READS,
     replaces: [],
     plan(spec, entry, view, env) {
       const hits = readEvents(entry, view, env, DEAL_READS).slice(0, FX_MOTIF_DEAL_MAX);
       const first = hits[0];
       if (first === undefined) return [];
       const t = timesOf(entry.durationMs);
       const from = dealtFrom(first.event, view, env);
       const cues: FxCue[] = [];
       if (from !== null) cues.push(motifBurst(spec, from, "point", t.G, MOTIF_TUNING.gather));
       for (const h of hits) {
         if (flies(from, h.at)) cues.push({ kind: "ghost", from, to: h.at, delayMs: t.T, durationMs: t.L - t.T });
         cues.push(motifBurst(spec, h.at, "point", t.L, MOTIF_TUNING.small, "sparkle"));
       }
       return cues;
     },
   };
   ```
   Then add `deal` to the `./hand.ts` import and to `MOTIF_PLANNERS` in `index.ts`.

4. **`motifs/gallery.ts`**:
   - Add `case "deal": return [{ type: "addedToHand", player, instanceId: "fx-dealt", defId: "core-055" }, { type: "shuffledIn", player, instanceId: "hidden", defId: "hidden", position: 0 }];` to `motifFixture`, and add a sentence about it to its doc comment.
   - Add the following exports, each with a one-line doc comment citing R2795000:
     - `export type GalleryCard = { defId: string; label: string; hook: FxCardHook | "bespoke" | "setPiece"; fixture: DrawnMotif | CardRecipeKey; spec: FxHookSpec | null }`.
     - `galleryCardOf(defId, entry: FxCardEntry): GalleryCard | null`, with these cases in order:
       - `none` → `null`.
       - `setPiece` → `{ label: "set piece: <key>", hook: "setPiece", fixture: "wipe", spec: null }`.
       - `bespoke` whose key passes `isCardRecipeKey` → `{ label: "bespoke: <key>", hook: "bespoke", fixture: key, spec: null }`; an entrance key → `null`.
       - `hooks` → the first hook in `FX_CARD_HOOKS` whose motif passes `isDrawnMotif`, as `{ label: "<hook>: <motif>", hook, fixture: motif, spec }`; if no hook qualifies → `null`.
     - `recipeFixture(key: CardRecipeKey, view, sourceId, player): GameEvent[]`, an exhaustive `switch` with no `default` (`enemy` is the other side, as `motifFixture` computes it):
       - `manaCrack`: `[{ type: "modifierChanged", player: enemy.player, modifierId: FX_NEXT_REFRESH_MODIFIER_ID, added: true }]`.
       - `bloodDrain`: `[{ type: "radiantSet", instanceId: "hidden", defId: "hidden", zone: { z: "hand", player } }, { type: "healthLost", player, amount: 3 }]`.
       - `crushingWalls`: `motifFixture("wipe", …)`.
       - `rollbackSweep`: `[{ type: "rolledBack", player, turnsAgo: 1, sides: [view.you.player, view.opponent.player] }]`.
       - `inkTear`: two `discarded` events (`fx-discarded-1` with `core-055`, `fx-discarded-2` with `core-002`), each `owner: enemy.player`.
       - `constantStamp`: one `numberChanged` (`key: "cost"`, `value: 3`) on `view.you.hand[0]`, or `[]` when there is no such card.
     - `galleryCardEvents(card, view, n = 0)`: `cardPlayed`, then (setPiece only) `{ type: "hookResolving", sourceId: instanceId, defId, controller: player, hook: "cry" }`, then the fixture (`recipeFixture` when `isCardRecipeKey(card.fixture)`, else `motifFixture`), then `cardResolved`. Use `instanceId = galleryPlayId(n)` and `player = view.viewer`, and copy the payloads of `cardFixtureEvents`. Then delete `cardFixtureEvents`.
     - `galleryHookCues(card, view, intensity, speed = 1): FxCue[]`. Return `[]` when `card.spec` is null or the fixture is a recipe. Otherwise compute the look and scale exactly as `planCardMotif` does: `paletteLook(spec.palette)` ?? `flavorLookOf(defId, GALLERY_CARD_ID, view)` ?? `FLAVOR_LOOKS[FLAVOR_FALLBACK]`, and `motifScale(defId, view, intensity)`. Then `planMotif` over `galleryEntry(motifFixture(...gallerySource(view)...), view, speed)` with a fresh memory, as `galleryCues` does.
     - `galleryShownView(view, card, n = 0): PlayerView`: `{ ...view, events: galleryCardEvents(...) }`. When `CATALOG[defId].type` is `"Field Spell"` or `"Field Trap"` and `view.you.backrow[0]` is face-up, also replace that slot with `{ ...slot, defId, instanceId: galleryPlayId(n), type }`, so its aura shows.

5. **`routes/dev/fx.tsx`**:
   - `galleryCards()` returns `(GalleryCard & { name: string })[]` from `galleryCardOf` over `FX_CARD_TABLE`.
